WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.060
The long wait for Wonder Woman 1984 is almost
over, and you can feel the excitement of the

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:07.089
cast and crew.

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:12.510
A virtual panel discussion for the much-anticipated
sequel kicked off the DC FanDome event with

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:19.200
a bang on August 22, as Gal Gadot, Chris Pine,
Kristen Wiig, Pedro Pascal, and director Patty

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:23.740
Jenkins fielded questions from fans across
the globe, including some wonderful surprise

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:24.560
guests.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.580
Jenkins and her cast reminisced fondly about
their time on set together, which must feel

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:34.550
almost as long ago as Diana's adventures in
World War I, after all the delays Wonder Woman

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.920
1984 has seen.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.680
Afterward, tennis legend and Wonder Woman
superfan Venus Williams joined in to ask Gadot

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.000
and Wiig which of their characters would win
in a tennis match.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.820
"I think Cheetah would win."

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:48.700
"Really?"

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.760
While this celebrity game of superhero what-if
was nothing short of delightful, an even more

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.800
special guest was waiting in the wings.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.299
Before debuting a brand-new trailer for Wonder
Woman 1984, the FanDome panel welcomed the

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:09.120
original on-screen Wonder Woman herself, the
iconic former beauty queen Lynda Carter.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:14.420
Despite the distance between the panel participants,
emotions ran high in the virtual Hall of Heroes

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.740
as two generations of Amazons expressed their
appreciation for each other.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.440
Carter explained that she and Wiig have a
mutual appreciation, which they intend to

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.460
seal with a hug as soon as they can be in
the same room, and gushed with praise for

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:31.240
Jenkins and Gadot's take on Diana of Themyscira.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:37.119
Carter became a TV icon during her three seasons
on the late '70s Wonder Woman series, and

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:41.240
she couldn't be happier that a whole new generation
is looking up to a whole new Diana Prince

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:42.200
on the big screen.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:46.479
She's seen first-hand what the character means
to fans of the movies, with her own daughter

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:51.219
falling under the spell of Gadot's Wonder
Woman, telling her, quote, "I finally get

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.080
what Wonder Woman means to everyone."

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:56.220
"She said, 'Mom, I finally get it.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:02.600
I finally understand why everyone idolizes
you.'"

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:07.539
Wonder Woman 1984 not only takes place in
a different era than the original flick did,

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.960
but it also shows a new side of the lasso-swinging
hero.

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.471
This time around, Diana has literal decades
of experience living in the world of man,

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.900
and she uses that wisdom to her benefit.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.920
In a cover story back in June, Gadot told
Total Film,

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.140
"In Wonder Woman 1984, she's been around.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.120
She's wiser.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.280
She's more mature.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:28.240
She's guarded.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.040
She lost all of her friends throughout the
years.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:32.820
But she's still doing the right thing.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:35.560
But she is different than when we last saw
her."

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:41.740
In the upcoming sequel, Diana's beloved Steve
Trevor, played by Chris Pine, is back after

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.020
having presumably died a true hero's death
in the first movie.

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:50.720
A new face is Barbara Ann Minerva, played
by Kristen Wiig, an archeologist who works

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:56.060
alongside Diana and even forms a friendship
with her...only to turn into Diana's foe after

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:58.600
a mishap grants her the powers of a cheetah.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:04.180
Then there's Pedro Pascal's Maxwell Lord,
a smarmy businessman with a villainous edge

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.320
who makes grandiose promises about granting
everyone's wishes.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:14.480
In the new trailer for Wonder Woman 1984 that
also dropped during DC FanDome, fans saw Lord

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:18.970
giving a speech from within what appeared
to be the White House Briefing Room, and also

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:22.640
spotted him having a conversation with Barbara
on Air Force One.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:28.220
This has led many fans to believe that Lord
perhaps wins a presidential election, using

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:32.520
his mysterious, wish-granting artifact to
either grant the public's wishes in exchange

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:36.200
for their votes or to grant his own wish for
more power.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:41.920
The sequel pic features a handful of actors
in yet-undisclosed roles, including Natasha

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:47.920
Rothwell of Saturday Night Live and Insecure
fame, Grandfathered star Ravi Patel, and Mad

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:52.840
Men actor Kristoffer Polaha, so there's no
telling how many more allies or antagonists

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.040
Diana will face in this next adventure.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:04:00.140
In all, it's looking like Wonder Woman 1984
will be a more-than-worthy follow-up flick

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.920
to the widely adored original.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.820
Catch the film on October 2nd, 2020.

